In this corrected code, I moved the debug statements inside the functions, I corrected the assertions for the remove method and some others, and I eliminated the unnecessary old and new array list count statements since their values are already contained in arrList.Count inside the function's body. I also replaced the obsolete using directives with the appropriate namespaces to avoid any compilation issues. The code remains readable and consistent with original C# syntax.

Remember to include this namespace: using System.Collections.Generic; since ArrayList class is not native to C#, even though it's a commonly used data structure, but is actually provided by the System.Collections.Generic namespace in C#.--------------------
